loyments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/deployments","created_at":"2014-06-12T16:00:38Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T22:36:14Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-12T23:00:16Z","git_url":"git://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:bazelbuild/bazel.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel","homepage":"https://bazel.build","size":993004,"stargazers_count":24886,"watchers_count":24886,"language":"Java","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":4359,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":1818,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["bazel","build","build-system","correct","fast","multi-language","scalable","test"],"visibility":"public","forks":4359,"open_issues":1818,"watchers":24886,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"> ATTENTION! Please read and follow:\r\n> - if this is a _question_ about how to build / test / query / deploy using Bazel, or a _discussion starter_, send it to bazel-discuss@googlegroups.com\r\n> - if this is a _bug_ or _feature request_, fill the form below as best as you can.\r\n\r\n### Description of the problem / feature request:\r\n\r\nWhen attempting to generate a directory artifact in a location that _previously_ contained an explicitly-named file output, Bazel throws an I/O exception.\r\n\r\nThis can be resolved by running `bazel clean`, which is problematic because we are trying to train our developers to never do that.\r\n\r\n```\r\nERROR: /home/eric/git/bazel_repro/BUILD.bazel:9:12: Action some failed: I/O exception during sandboxed execution: Could not move output artifacts from sandboxed execution\r\nTarget //:new_rule failed to build\r\nUse --verbose_failures to see the command lines of failed build steps.\r\nINFO: Elapsed time: 0.230s, Critical Path: 0.07s\r\nINFO: 2 processes: 2 internal.\r\nFAILED: Build did NOT complete successfully\r\n```\r\n\r\nI originally encountered this bug in a persistent worker, which resulted in a much less readable error message but ultimately the same behavior.\r\n\r\n### Bugs: what's the simplest, easiest way to reproduce this bug? Please provide a minimal example if possible.\r\n\r\nCheck out this repo, https://github.com/HALtheWise/bazel-directory-failure, run `bazel build //...`, edit BUILD.bazel by switching which rule is commented out, then run `bazel build //...` again.\r\n\r\n### What operating system are you running Bazel on?\r\n\r\nUbuntu\r\n\r\n### What's the output of `bazel info release`?\r\n\r\n`release 4.0.0`\r\n\r\n###  Have you found anything relevant by searching the web?\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/2235 from four years ago seems similar\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/13233/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/13233/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":4483125323,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDQ0ODMxMjUzMjM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/events/4483125323","actor":{"login":"oquenchil","id":23365806,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzY1ODA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23365806?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oquenchil","html_url":"https://github.com/oquenchil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oquenchil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oquenchil/following{/other_user}","gists